# Documentation rules — PRIORITY

Docs are part of Done, not an afterthought. Read `.agents/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md`.

## Every change updates docs
- **New feature** → write/extend a guide in `docs/guides/` and/or API doc in `docs/api/`.
- **Architectural decision** → new **ADR** in `docs/adr/` using the ADR template, with an
  **incrementing number** (`NNNN-title.md`). Record context, decision, consequences.
- **User-facing change** → add an entry to `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog format, under `[Unreleased]`).
- **Runbooks** for operational/debug procedures go in `docs/runbooks/`; architecture notes in `docs/architecture/`.

## How to write
- Document **WHY**, not just WHAT. Explain decisions, trade-offs, and non-obvious behavior.
- Keep docs **in sync with code** — update them in the same change, not later.
- Create docs/folders proactively when a topic needs them. Keep cross-links (README ↔ docs) valid.

## Checklist before declaring done
- [ ] Relevant guide/API doc updated or created.
- [ ] ADR added if a decision was made.
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` updated for user-facing changes.
- [ ] `plan/PLAN.md` updated (see plan-management rule).
